# Customer-specific compliance scoping (NEVER commit to public repo).
# These artefacts map the customer-agnostic docs/DEVELOPMENT_LIFECYCLE.md
# to a specific buyer's framework requirements (e.g. MOD/Defence JSPs,
# DART/CAAT registers, DefStan 00-055). Keep local. The customer-
# agnostic SDLC doc stays the public surface.
_mod_*.md
_mod_*.pdf
_mod_*.html
_mod_*.csv

# PDF build artefacts (regenerable from .md sources)
tools/pdf_build/_build/
tools/pdf_build/_test/

# Export bundle (regenerable; MOD-local content lives inside)
export/

# Generated PDFs at the repo root and under docs/ — all regenerable
# from the .md sources via tools/pdf_build/. Never commit a PDF to
# the repo; the source of truth is markdown.
*.pdf

# Per-export docs/impex/ bundle (regenerable export, often customer-
# scoped). Mirrors content already present under docs/ as markdown.
docs/impex/

# Local-only test scripts (not part of the shipped image — these
# stay on the developer workstation only).
.local-*
seed_test_data.py

# Workspace-specific MCP server configuration (per-developer; lists
# local servers like pentest-mcp that aren't shared in the repo).
.mcp.json

# Claude Code project context — contains internal architecture detail,
# development notes, and system references that should not be public.
CLAUDE.md

# Internal working documents (planning, specs, research, handoffs).
# Committed in v0.31.16 for local reference; excluded from public repo
# going forward. Existing history entries remain in git log.
_handoff_v*.md
_spec_v*.md
_backlog_v*.md
_research_*.md

# v0.38.0: pre-built briefing-deck assets ship in the image — keep the PDFs
!src/ion/web/static/briefings/*.pdf
# deck build scratch (node deps + intermediate HTML)
.deck_build/
.playwright-mcp/
